<Layout title="What is SEO for a small business? | Virgil Digital" description="A plain-English explanation of SEO, how search engines rank websites, and what small businesses can do to become more visible.">
  <span class="kicker">Guide · Search visibility</span><h1>What SEO actually <span class="accent">means.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">SEO is the work of making the right information easy for search engines and people to find, understand, trust, and act on.</p>
  <h2>How search works</h2><p>Search engines discover pages, read their content, understand what each page is about, and decide which results are most useful for a particular search. They consider relevance, quality, technical accessibility, location, reputation, and the meaning behind the query.</p>
  <h2>What helps a small business</h2><p>Clear service pages, accurate contact details, useful answers, descriptive page titles, fast mobile pages, a maintained Google Business Profile, genuine reviews, and links from relevant websites all help build a clearer picture of the business.</p>
  <h2>What SEO cannot promise</h2><p>No honest person can guarantee a specific ranking or a fixed number of enquiries. Competition, location, search demand, and changes in the search results all matter. Good SEO is a sustained improvement process, not a switch you turn on.</p>
  <h2>Where to start</h2><p>Make sure your website says exactly what you do, where you do it, who it is for, and how to contact you. Then make sure those details agree across your Google listing and social profiles.</p>
